{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13653","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13653/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13653/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13653/events","html_url":"https://github.com/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/issues/13653","id":1341334029,"node_id":"I_kwDOBlCVUc5P8yIN","number":13653,"title":"[CDCSDK] Deleting stream IDs lead to stale entries in the cdc_state table causing tserver crash","user":{"login":"fourpointfour","id":34186745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MTg2NzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34186745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour","html_url":"https://github.com/fourpointfour","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fourpointfour/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":711841622,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MTE4NDE2MjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/labels/kind/bug","name":"kind/bug","color":"c2e0c6","default":false,"description":"This issue is a bug"},{"id":1419821900,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNDE5ODIxOTAw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/labels/priority/medium","name":"priority/medium","color":"ffdc5e","default":false,"description":"Medium priority issue"},{"id":3108235291,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMTA4MjM1Mjkx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yugabyte/yugabyte-db/labels/area/cdcsdk","name":"area/cdcsdk","color":"6C1C93","default":false,"description":"CDC SDK"}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2022-08-17T07:51:12Z","updated_at":"2024-06-29T09:44:03Z","closed_at":"2022-08-22T15:19:39Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [DB-3219](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-3219)\r\nWhat’s happening is that in case a `stream_id` is deleted, the metadata related to it is not getting cleared from the `cdc_state` table - and now even if a new stream is created, the previous (deleted) stream is causing interference to the functioning which is ultimately leading to a tserver crash.\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce:\r\n1. Create a table\r\n2. Create stream ID using `yb-admin create_change_data_stream ysql.<namespace-name>`\r\n3. Deploy the DBZ connector config\r\n4. Delete the DBZ connector config\r\n5. Delete the stream ID using `yb-admin delete_change_data_stream <stream-id>`\r\n6. Create another table\r\n7. Create a new stream ID\r\n8. Deploy the connector config using the stream created in *step 7* - you will see a tserver crash\r\n\r\nHowever, there is a workaround which has been identified to unblock the users i.e.\r\n1. Set the GFlag `yb_system_namespace_readonly` to `false`\r\n2. Using `ycqlsh` delete the entries corresponding to the deleted stream ID in *step 5*","closed_by":{"login":"yugabyte-ci","id":17281578,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxNTc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17281578?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"